Third-party components and prototype integrations
================================================

Java runtime: OpenJDK 21, Eclipse Temurin images. OpenJDK is GPL v2 with the
Classpath Exception; image-specific distribution notices remain in the images.
Exact build/runtime image digests are recorded in code/app/backend/Dockerfile.

Spring Boot 4.1.1 and managed Spring Framework, Spring Security, Spring Data,
Spring MVC and Thymeleaf integration: Apache License 2.0, except transitive
components with their own notices. Exact managed versions are fixed by the
Spring Boot parent BOM in code/app/backend/pom.xml.

Thymeleaf: Apache License 2.0.
Hibernate ORM: GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1.
Flyway Community: Apache License 2.0.
PostgreSQL JDBC driver: BSD 2-Clause License.
PostgreSQL 17 (Docker image): PostgreSQL License; image notices also apply.
Jackson: Apache License 2.0.
Nimbus JOSE + JWT: Apache License 2.0.
Apache Maven 3.10.0 / Maven Wrapper 3.3.4: Apache License 2.0.
JUnit, Mockito, AssertJ and Spring test dependencies are development/test tools;
their respective licenses are supplied with their distributions.

No CDN or paid API is required by the Java cabinet. HTML, CSS and JavaScript
assets are repository-local; fonts fall back to installed system fonts.

Python 3.13.7, FastAPI 0.146.0 (MIT), Pydantic 2.13.4 (MIT),
SQLAlchemy 2.0.55 (MIT), asyncpg 0.32.0 (Apache 2.0), Uvicorn 0.53.0
(BSD 3-Clause), httpx 0.28.1 (BSD 3-Clause), greenlet 3.5.6 (MIT/Python),
CatBoost 1.2.10 (Apache 2.0), NumPy 2.5.4, pandas 3.0.6,
SciPy 1.18.1, scikit-learn 1.9.1, joblib 1.6.0 and threadpoolctl 3.7.0
(BSD-style upstream licenses). Transitive runtime components and artifact hashes
are fixed in code/scorer/requirements-service.lock. Matplotlib and its upstream
license/notices are included as CatBoost dependencies. No notebook execution or
training dependencies beyond the selected inference stack are required at startup.

Model: selected CatBoost regressor, trained by the project on synthetic company
applications. The delivery rebuild uses the existing selected configuration and
8,000-row development split; the 2,000-row reused holdout is diagnostic only.
Source, feature/data hashes and measured diagnostic error are recorded in
code/scorer/artifacts/selected_model.validation.json. This is not a real default
probability model or independently validated banking decision system.

Data: development accounts, companies, report examples and test fixtures are
synthetic project data. No real customer, bureau or bank records are included.
Development RSA keys and demo passwords are public test fixtures, not production
credentials.

Integrations and simplifications:
- Python scorer: supplied FastAPI service applies the real saved CatBoost model.
  No dummy provider, generated scoring answer or fallback model is included.
- EGRUL/EGRIP, FNS and credit bureaus: no live or simulated external calls in the
  Java branch. Company profile fields are declared information, not verified
  source responses. Future integration must preserve this distinction.
- Financial documents: structured JSON schema/value consistency checks, not OCR
  or verification of arbitrary statements. Prototype document bytes live in DB.
- Signing and disbursement: explicitly labelled state transitions only; no legal
  signature, payment rail or transfer is performed.
- Credit policy: simplified product/age/affordability rules, not bank policy.
- No LLM or closed-weight model is used in the Java runtime.

This inventory does not replace the license texts distributed with dependencies.
